@*
    OdsModal — the dialog shell (Odyssey Design System · components/Modal).

    Scrim, header (title + optional subtitle + close), scrollable body, and a
    right-aligned footer for actions. An inline MudDialog bound to Open
    (@bind-Open). Wide is the 1240px / 96vw variant for batch grids / file
    analysis. OnClose fires on Esc, scrim click, and the close button; omit it
    (leave Open one-way) to hide the close affordance.

    Field markers: the system marks REQUIRED only (a `*` after the label) — nothing
    is ever labelled "Optional". The dialog explains the asterisk once: when the
    body holds at least one required field, the footer grows a muted "* Required"
    legend on the left. Detection is by what actually rendered (a CSS :has() over
    the body for .odc-field-req / MudBlazor's .mud-input-required), so no host has
    to declare it and a field that appears conditionally is picked up live. Pass
    RequiredLegend="false" to suppress it.

    Steps (Odyssey Design System · Modal `steps`, version 1795477868-c9a2) makes it a WIZARD dialog: an
    OdsWizardSteps placed in the slot renders as a full-width row under the title (`has-steps` head), the
    surface widens to 760px with roomier padding (`wizard`), and the footer wraps (Back and an error summary
    join Cancel and the primary). One dialog: one title, one draft, one Cancel.

    Focus is set ONCE per opening (the open edge in OnParametersSet), never on a re-render, so typing in a
    field never moves focus. Only the TOP dialog answers Esc and traps Tab: MudBlazor binds its key
    interceptor to each dialog's own container element and its focus trap to that container's sentinels,
    and stacked dialogs are sibling containers in the provider, so a key in the dialog on top never reaches
    the one beneath (pinned by ModalStackTests). No extra stack is kept here.

    Dismissible="false" (issue #509 §4.1) takes Escape, the scrim and the close
    button away while a dialog must not close — a request in flight. It is turned
    off BEFORE MudDialog can close itself, which a guard in OnClose could not do,
    and it is re-applied to the open dialog whenever it changes, so a host can go
    busy and back without re-opening.
*@

@implements IAsyncDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime Js

<MudDialog @ref="_dialog" @key="Wide" Visible="@Open" VisibleChanged="OnVisibleChanged" Options="_options"
           Class="@($"ods-modal {ModalKey}{(Steps is null ? "" : " wizard")} {Class}".TrimEnd())"
           ContentClass="@(HideHeader ? null : "ods-modal-content")"
           TitleClass="@(Steps is null ? "ods-modal-head" : "ods-modal-head has-steps")"
           ActionsClass="ods-modal-foot"
           TitleContent="@(HideHeader ? null : HeaderFragment)"
           AriaLabel="@EffectiveAriaLabel">
    <DialogContent>
        <OdsModalInstanceProbe Register="OnInstance" />
        @ChildContent
    </DialogContent>
    <DialogActions>
        @if (RequiredLegend)
        {
            <span class="ods-modal-legend"><span class="odc-field-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span> Required</span>
        }
        @Footer
    </DialogActions>
</MudDialog>

@code {
    // The fragment is the inner content of MudDialog's title slot, which carries
    // ods-modal-head (the tinted band + flex layout). Children: an optional lead
    // tile, the title/subtitle stack, then the close button pushed to the edge.
    private RenderFragment HeaderFragment => @<text>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Icon))
        {
            <div class="@($"ods-modal-lead {ToneClass}".TrimEnd())">
                @if (IsLigature(Icon))
                {
                    <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">@Icon</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    @* A non-ligature glyph (e.g. "§") — rendered as type, not an icon-font
                       ligature, mirroring the design-system Modal lead-tile glyph path. *@
                    <span class="ods-modal-lead-glyph" aria-hidden="true">@Icon</span>
                }
            </div>
        }
        <div class="ods-modal-titles">
            @if (Title is not null)
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="@TitleTag" Class="ods-modal-title">@Title</MudText>
            }
            @if (Subtitle is not null)
            {
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Default" Class="ods-modal-sub mud-text-secondary">@Subtitle</MudText>
            }
        </div>
        @HeaderActions
        @if (CanDismiss)
        {
            <OdsIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Close" Size="OdsSize.Sm"
                           AriaLabel="Close" OnClick="CloseAsync" Class="ods-modal-x" />
        }
        @if (Steps is not null)
        {
            @* The wizard's step path: a full-width row under the title, in the header band, so it never
               scrolls away with the body (Odyssey Design System · Modal `steps`). *@
            <div class="ods-modal-steps">@Steps</div>
        }
    </text>;
}
